The '''Baliscan Selective Service''' ({{lang-bl|Servicio Selectivo de Baliscano}}; '''SSB''') is the {{W|public service}} and {{W|job guarantee}} program of the [[Balisca|Baliscan Confederation]], and is considered to be a ''de facto'' {{W|social integration}} initiative in the country. Originally created in 1929 in a push for economic planning after [[Baliscan Revolution|the Revolution]], and expanded during the [[Adonian Depression]], it is open to all residents of Balisca (including immigrants and non-citizens who have resided in the country for at least 1 year) that are over the age of 18.

Mandatory from 1929 to 1983, participation in the Selective Service is now entirely optional. Participation in the Selective Service by a non-citizen entitles them to various [[social protection in Balisca|social protection]] programs and benefits, including job training, Baliscano courses, communal employment, and a shortened {{W|naturalization}} process (which entitles them to the [[Social Housing Scheme (Balisca)|Social Housing Scheme]] and the [[Cooperative Housing Scheme (Balisca)|Cooperative Housing Scheme]]). Depending on the branch, service can last from a minimum of 12 months to a maximum of 60 months. Upon the completion of the mandatory period, individuals have the choice of discharge or an extension in service. 

As of 1 May 2023, 62.6 percent of the Selective Service is made up of non-citizens, which is reflective of both its status as the fastest path to Baliscan citizenship and increasing {{W|refusal to work|rejection of work}} among Baliscan youth.

Since 1976, all Baliscan students in {{W|Twelfth grade|Year 14}} (the final year prior to university) of their education are offered to take the [[Confederal Aptitude Test]], a standardized exam that is widely considered to be {{W|High-stakes testing|high-stakes}} and is required for acceptance into the service. Individuals are afforded one optional retake prior to their entrance into the service, with the individual's preference of the two results being taken into consideration. The test contains five categories which take into account the individual's {{W|self-fulfillment}} aspirations and attempt to match their abilities to the most suitable service.  

